cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "FractureFlow: label-free structural-orientation statistics and honest machine-learning benchmarks for fracture data"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-29
license: MIT
authors:
  - given-names: "Jiacheng"
    family-names: "Yi"
    email: "2998812494@qq.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/wansong42/fractureflow"
abstract: >-
  FractureFlow turns raw fracture observations (borehole logs, borehole-image
  logs, outcrop trace maps, dense point clouds) into structural-orientation
  statistics (set tables, rose diagrams, DFN screening) without requiring
  fracture-level ground-truth labels, and ships an honest evaluation harness
  with published negative results and information-ceiling measurements.
keywords:
  - fracture networks
  - structural geology
  - borehole image logs
  - discrete fracture network
  - label-free learning
